# FRENCH CHICKEN STEW
## info  
* About 20 minutes prep, 4 to 6 hours total
* about 6 servings  

## ingredients
* 3 pounds boneless, skinless chicken thighs, trimmed
* Salt and pepper
* 1/4 cup vegetable oil
* 2 onions, minced
* 6 garlic cloves, minced
* 1 tablespoon tomato paste
* 2 teaspoons minced fresh thyme or 1/2 teaspoon dried
* 1/3 cup all-purpose flour
* 1/2 cup dry white wine
* 4 cups low-sodium chicken broth, plus extra as needed
* 12 ounces red potatoes (2-3 medium), scrubbed and cut into 1/2-inch pieces
* 4 carrots, peeled and sliced 1/4 inch thick
* 2 bay leaves
* 1 cup frozen peas
* 1/4 cup minced fresh parsley

## steps  
1. Dry chicken with paper towels and season with salt and pepper.
1. Heat 1 tablespoon vegetable oil in a 12-inch skillet over medium-high heat until just smoking.
1. Brown half the chicken lightly on both sides, 5 to 8 minutes; transfer to a bowl. Repeat with another tablespoon of oil and the remaining chicken, then transfer to the bowl.
1. Heat the remaining tablespoon of oil over medium-high heat until shimmering. Add onions, garlic, tomato paste, and thyme and cook until onions are softened and lightly browned, about 8 to 10 minutes.
1. Stir in flour and cook for 1 minute. Slowly whisk in wine, scraping up any browned bits.
1. Whisk in 1 cup of broth, smoothing out any lumps, then transfer the mixture to a slow cooker.
1. Microwave potatoes and carrots with the remaining tablespoon of oil in a covered bowl, stirring occasionally, until vegetables are nearly tender, about 5 minutes. Transfer to the slow cooker.
1. Stir in the remaining 3 cups broth, peas, and bay leaves into the slow cooker. Nestle the browned chicken and any accumulated juices into the stew.
1. Cover and cook until the chicken is tender, 4 to 6 hours on low.
1. Transfer chicken to a cutting board, let cool slightly, then shred into bite-sized pieces.
1. Let the stew settle for 5 minutes, then remove any fat from the surface with a large spoon. Discard bay leaves.
1. Stir shredded chicken into the stew. Adjust consistency with additional hot broth as needed. Stir in parsley and season with salt and pepper.

## notes  
* Browning the chicken before slow cooking builds richer flavor.
* If the stew becomes too thick, add hot broth until it reaches the desired consistency.

